WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.400 --> 00:00:02.667
-Good evening. I'm Seth Meyers.

00:00:02.667 --> 00:00:04.133
This is "Late Night."
We hope you're doing well.

00:00:04.133 --> 00:00:05.300
And now, if you don't mind,
we're going to get to the news.

00:00:05.300 --> 00:00:08.133
Former President Trump's
attorney Joe Tacopina

00:00:08.133 --> 00:00:10.200
said in a new interview
that it was a, quote,

00:00:10.200 --> 00:00:13.200
"relief" to see the final
charges against Trump.

00:00:13.200 --> 00:00:17.501
Alright, you know it's bad
when 34 felonies is a relief.

00:00:17.501 --> 00:00:22.100
Phew, really dodged
a bullet there.

00:00:22.100 --> 00:00:23.801
After attending a rally
in Manhattan

00:00:23.801 --> 00:00:25.801
in support of former
President Trump on Tuesday,

00:00:25.801 --> 00:00:27.667
Georgia Congresswoman
Marjorie Taylor Greene

00:00:27.667 --> 00:00:29.634
criticized New York
during an interview

00:00:29.634 --> 00:00:31.300
with Fox News host
Tucker Carlson

00:00:31.300 --> 00:00:33.501
and said, "I think
it's a very terrible place."

00:00:33.501 --> 00:00:35.968
But the joke's on you,
Marjorie,

00:00:35.968 --> 00:00:39.501
because once you think that,
you're officially a New Yorker.

00:00:39.501 --> 00:00:42.033
[ Laughter ]

00:00:42.033 --> 00:00:44.534
After he was arraigned
on Tuesday in Manhattan,

00:00:44.534 --> 00:00:45.734
Former President Trump
reportedly

00:00:45.734 --> 00:00:48.033
sat on the patio at Mar-a-Lago

00:00:48.033 --> 00:00:51.100
and used his iPad to play music
over the club's speakers,

00:00:51.100 --> 00:00:54.067
including "Macho Man"
by the Village People.

00:00:54.067 --> 00:00:56.367
"Hey man, you can't play
that here anymore,"

00:00:56.367 --> 00:00:58.534
said the governor
of Florida.

00:00:58.534 --> 00:01:01.067
[ Laughter ]

00:01:01.067 --> 00:01:03.968
According to a new report
from the EPA,

00:01:03.968 --> 00:01:06.033
there are more than
1 million lead pipes

00:01:06.033 --> 00:01:07.467
still in use in Florida.

00:01:07.467 --> 00:01:10.133
And there are actually
more than that in New Jersey,

00:01:10.133 --> 00:01:13.200
but they don't want
to have to use them.

00:01:13.200 --> 00:01:15.434
[ Laughter ]

00:01:15.434 --> 00:01:18.634
You know what I mean?

00:01:18.634 --> 00:01:20.767
Lamborghini this week
unveiled its first

00:01:20.767 --> 00:01:22.534
plug-in hybrid supercar.

00:01:22.534 --> 00:01:25.334
Now you can help save
the planet for your children

00:01:25.334 --> 00:01:27.567
from all three
of your marriages.

00:01:27.567 --> 00:01:30.300
[ Laughter ]

00:01:30.300 --> 00:01:31.968
A government official
in Singapore

00:01:31.968 --> 00:01:34.200
was recently sentenced
to two years in jail

00:01:34.200 --> 00:01:35.601
after he allegedly
sold more than

00:01:35.601 --> 00:01:38.367
600 stolen printer cartridges
online.

00:01:38.367 --> 00:01:42.501
No word on what happened to the
trillions of dollars he made.

00:01:45.300 --> 00:01:47.033
I'm from the generation
where we had to buy

00:01:47.033 --> 00:01:49.033
our own printer cartridge.

00:01:49.033 --> 00:01:50.767
They get you on the cyan?

00:01:50.767 --> 00:01:52.167
Is that the one
they get you on, Baze?

00:01:52.167 --> 00:01:53.767
Yeah.

00:01:57.033 --> 00:01:58.501
According to a new survey,

00:01:58.501 --> 00:02:00.868
an estimated
44 million American adults

00:02:00.868 --> 00:02:02.767
are experiencing
significant loneliness,

00:02:02.767 --> 00:02:04.968
which explains why they were
willing to take a survey.

00:02:04.968 --> 00:02:10.133
"No, it's not.
It's not a bad time at all."

00:02:10.133 --> 00:02:12.334
A person walking
on a beach in Florida

00:02:12.334 --> 00:02:15.200
recently found a 30-pound
bale of marijuana,

00:02:15.200 --> 00:02:17.067
and they admittedly
did the right thing

00:02:17.067 --> 00:02:20.701
and reported the 25-pound
bale of marijuana.

00:02:24.501 --> 00:02:25.834
According to a new study,

00:02:25.834 --> 00:02:28.434
poor sleep can increase
the risk of a stroke.

00:02:28.434 --> 00:02:31.133
But on the plus side,
you got to hear this joke.

00:02:31.133 --> 00:02:33.267
[ Light laughter ]

00:02:38.934 --> 00:02:40.968
Two former prison guards
in Oklahoma

00:02:40.968 --> 00:02:43.100
were recently sentenced
to probation for allegedly

00:02:43.100 --> 00:02:47.100
forcing inmates to listen to the
song "Baby Shark" as punishment.

00:02:47.100 --> 00:02:51.067
And it's worse than you think,
because they played it twice.

00:02:53.400 --> 00:02:55.501
That's right, two former
prison guards in Oklahoma

00:02:55.501 --> 00:02:57.667
were recently sentenced
to probation for allegedly

00:02:57.667 --> 00:03:01.300
forcing inmates to listen
to the song "Baby Shark."

00:03:01.300 --> 00:03:03.634
Meanwhile, a local charity
in New York

00:03:03.634 --> 00:03:07.234
remains unpunished.

00:03:07.234 --> 00:03:10.133
And that was a monologue,
everybody.

